    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0252" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg136"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/932.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to Great Britain to the
                        Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 10, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Langley says that the British Government will admit the special rights of Russia
                    and Japan in the regions of Manchuria and Mongolia, but would at the same time
                    affirm the policy of the open door. Langley will at once communicate to Sir
                    Edward Grey your suggestion as to reaching an understanding before the meeting
                    of the 15th.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reid.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
